# Shell scripts are checked out with LF everywhere.  build.yml's install-windows runs
# scripts/check_rerun.sh from a `bash -l {0}` step on windows-latest (Git-Bash),
# and a CRLF `set -euo pipefail\r` fails that shell before it does anything.
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, so "it works
# today" is not evidence -- this rule is what makes it not matter.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher must ship BYTE FOR BYTE: scripts/pack.sh copies it into
# the package and `cmp`s the copy.  It is CRLF (since 2026-11-01; LF before):
# cmd.exe can miss a `goto`/`call` label in an LF-only batch file, depending on
# where the label falls.  This rule stops git normalising it in EITHER direction.
# Kept last because git's last matching rule wins, so a future `*` rule above
# cannot reach it.
#
# The recipe GENERATES the .bat link hooks at build time; nothing here touches
# those, and the recipe asserts their line endings itself.
*.bat -text
